PHP mistyping bug
This PHP script attempts to show you that PHP does crazy type interpretations
based on the first couple of characters.  If a string begins with what looks
like a number (i.e. two consecutive ASCII numbers), it interprets the string
as a number until it reaches a non-numeric ASCII character and returns an
integer value.  The exact same string, when passed to a string function like 
strstr, is interpreted as a string not an integer.  Thus, for strstr, you
can pass the test by putting "iloveyou" at the end of the password and
for the "> 10" test, you put in a two digit number.

